    "q-91627": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91627",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Adam has a bag with $\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{oz}$ of candy. If he has eaten $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the candy in the bag, how many ounces of candy did Adam eat?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out the weight of candy Adam ate, we need to calculate $\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{7}{3}.$\n\nTo multiply the two numbers, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{7}{3}=\\frac{3\\times 7}{4\\times 3}=\\frac{21}{12}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{21}{12}=\\frac{21÷3}{12÷3}=\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nSo, Adam ate $\\frac{7}{4}\\,\\text{oz}$ of candy.",
